--TEST--
`prepareRename` on an interface's own declaration answers the range of its name, because a type declared in the workspace is renamed everywhere it is written, `rule:ide/no-refactoring-introduces-an-alias`
--FILE--
<?nvs
interface Gre<|>ets
{
    public function greet(): string;
}

class User implements Greets
{
    public function greet(): string
    {
        return "hi";
    }
}
--REQUEST--
prepareRename
--EXPECT--
case.nvs:2:11-2:17
